D. PARITY MAPPING (web SavingsCalculator.tsx → native)
================================================================================
Data        : web is presentational (props: gasComparison|null, gasPrice, mpg, electricityRate,
              onChange×3, distanceUnit; hook useTranslation). Native binds the resolved charging
              aggregates via the P1/S8 SavingsCalculatorSource seam (no HTTP in the view) and OWNS the
              three assumption fields + Reset, recomputing GasComparison live on every edit — the
              parent hook's useMemo behavior, ported VERBATIM (gallons = dist/mpg, gasCost, evCost,
              monthly = (gas−ev)/months, yearly ×12, savings, costPerMile gas/EV; EV card surfaces
              actualCost). SI stays at the source/facade boundary; the view is unit-agnostic.
Composition : TSGlassPanel surface; header (calculator glyph + title + freshness/refresh accessory);
              responsive ViewThatFits(.horizontal) → "Your Assumptions" column (3 token fields with
              unit suffixes + Reset Defaults TSButton) beside the "Comparison" column (4 TSGlassPanel
              cards: Gas Cost / EV Cost / Total Savings / Monthly Savings).
States      : loading (skeleton grid) · empty ("Not enough data for comparison") · error (retry) ·
              stale (chip + auto-refresh) · offline (cached or message + retry) · content. The
              assumptions column renders in EVERY state — the surface is never blank.
i18n        : all 14 source t() keys present in SavingsCalculator.strings (table "SavingsCalculator")
              with web English fallbacks, + input suffixes + native chrome. No English literals in code.
a11y        : VoiceOver labels/values on every field + the combined comparison summary; decorative
              glyphs hidden; Dynamic Type (system fonts) + Reduce-Motion respected (TSSkeleton/TSButton).
Telemetry   : emits DashboardWidgetTelemetryEvent .viewOpened(surface:"SavingsCalculator") on .task
              (P1/S11). surfaceSlug + event asserted in tests.

